  "merits": "Second dua: This supplicatory prayer has been mentioned by Sayyid Ibn Tawus.\n\nZakat al-Fitrah: It is worth mentioning that Zakat al-Fitrah is one of the confirmed obligations, since the acceptance of one’s fasting is dependent upon the defrayment of this alms. It is also security against death up to the next year. In this verse of the Holy Qur’an, Almighty Allah has mentioned Zakat before the prayers: “He indeed shall be successful who pays Zakat, magnifies the name of his Lord, and prays. 87/14-15”\n\nSoil of Imam al-Husayn’s tomb: Shaykh al-Mufid has mentioned that it is advisable to swallow a piece of the soil of Imam al-Husayn’s tomb, for it is remedy for all illnesses.\n\nDuas for the ‘Id prayer: It is also recommended to say the supplicatory prayers that have been mentioned by Sayyid Ibn Tawus in Iqbal al-A’mal. Among these supplicatory prayers is the one that Abu-Hamzah al-Thumali has reported Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) as saying: When you ready yourself for joining the congregational Friday Prayers and the ‘Id Prayers, you may say this supplicatory prayer."
